1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,350
Welcome to Murmurent.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,210
In the next few minutes, you'll install it, tell it who you are,

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:12,840
and see how members, labs, and whole research centres connect
through the public hub.

4
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:20,760
Murmurent is shared agentic AI infrastructure for research, built on top
of Claude Code.

5
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:26,490
At its heart is a village of AI agents: specialists that live side by side,

6
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:29,850
follow shared rules, and work for every member.

7
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:33,310
The people stay organised the way they already are.

8
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:38,070
Individual members belong to groups: a lab, or a core facility,

9
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:42,330
each led by a PI Groups come together on projects.

10
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:46,460
And a centre's administration, run by a mayor, keeps the registry.

11
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:50,630
Every group keeps authority over its own people and its own data.

12
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,020
We call that choreography, not orchestration.

13
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:56,770
Here's the plan.

14
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,070
Install Murmurent, and check it.

15
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,560
Tell it who you are.

16
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:04,360
Make a project folder Murmurent-ready, and meet the agents.

17
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:09,330
Then join a lab or a centre, and find shared workflows in the public hub.

18
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:15,050
Before you start, you'll need a terminal on a Mac or Linux machine,

19
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:18,920
git, and Claude Code, installed and signed in.

20
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:21,690
You don't need to install Python yourself.

21
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:26,730
The installer fetches Python 3.12 if your system doesn't have it.

22
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,450
Step one: install.

23
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,276
The recommended route uses uv, a fast Python tool installer.

24
00:01:34,326 --> 00:01:37,000
If you don't have it yet, one line installs it.

25
00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:39,760
Then run: uv tool install murmurent.

26
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:43,370
Followed by: murmurent install.

27
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:47,152
That wires the shared agents, rules, and skills into Claude Code,

28
00:01:47,202 --> 00:01:54,290
registers the data-governance hooks, and creates your personal
identity key.

29
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:59,090
If your shell can't find the command afterwards, just open a new
terminal.

30
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:03,350
Step two: check the install.

31
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:07,380
murmurent doctor checks your Python, the agent, rule,

32
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:11,190
and skill links in Claude Code, and the registered hooks.

33
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:15,200
Every problem it finds comes with the one command that fixes it.

34
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:19,370
Run it any time, and again after every upgrade.

35
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:24,160
Step three: tell Murmurent who you are.

36
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:31,090
murmurent init records your handle, name, email, institutional handle,
GitHub, and Slack.

37
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:33,390
You'll pick one of three roles.

38
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:35,923
A member, who works in a lab or core.

39
00:02:35,973 --> 00:02:37,720
A PI, who leads one.

40
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:42,800
Or a mayor, who runs a centre made of many labs and cores.

41
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:46,670
murmurent whoami shows your handle and key, any time.

42
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:54,270
Step four: Murmurent works inside git repositories, kept under your
repos folder.

43
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:56,240
Ask first, with: murmurent repo status.

44
00:02:56,290 --> 00:02:59,940
A plain clone gets: repo adopt.

45
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:05,190
That adds a small marker file and links to the shared agents,

46
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,510
and leaves everything else untouched.

47
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,760
Commit both, so every clone is ready too.

48
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:14,990
A folder set up by an older release gets: repo upgrade.

49
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:18,520
When the verdict says ready, open Claude Code there.

50
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:24,310
Inside Claude Code, you'll meet the village itself: the commons,

51
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:29,070
a set of reference agents every member shares, each addressed by
name.

52
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:32,080
The Oracle is your personal research memory.

53
00:03:32,130 --> 00:03:35,140
The Bookworm handles literature and databases.

54
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:38,480
The Blacksmith does computation and statistics.

55
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:40,510
The Artist makes figures.

56
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,850
The Adversary audits your methods.

57
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,610
The Teacher explains things in plain words.

58
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:50,040
And the Conscience, the Lawyer, and the Security Guard review equity,

59
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:52,670
intellectual property, and secrets.

60
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:56,540
Every agent opens its reply with a one-line verdict.

61
00:03:58,090 --> 00:04:02,850
If your PI already runs Murmurent, joining their lab takes a few
commands.

62
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,860
You'll need to be in your lab's Slack workspace.

63
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:08,930
Run murmurent enroll, with your lab's name,

64
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:12,750
and send the request file to your PI by direct message.

65
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:17,670
They issue a signed member card, and send it back.

66
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:20,990
Before you import it, confirm the trust root, a short public key,

67
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:25,800
with your PI in person or by phone, not in the same message.

68
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:31,620
Then run import-card with that trust root, and whoami will show your
lab and role.

69
00:04:31,670 --> 00:04:36,470
Finally, clone your lab's governance repository to see the whole roster.

70
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:42,950
PIs joining a centre start at the public hub: murmurent_public, on
GitHub.

71
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,350
Find your institution in the directory.

72
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,420
Download and run the join script.

73
00:04:47,470 --> 00:04:53,250
It asks a few questions, encrypts your request to the centre's key, and
opens your email app.

74
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,180
Just press Send.

75
00:04:55,230 --> 00:04:59,200
Only the mayor can read it, and nothing about you is posted publicly.

76
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:02,990
Once they approve, you receive your PI ID Import it,

77
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:07,710
and you become your lab's certificate authority, issuing cards to your
own members.

78
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:12,760
Mayors set up a centre once, with murmurent centre-init,

79
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:15,500
giving just a name and an institution.

80
00:05:15,550 --> 00:05:19,120
Then, centre-hub-publish lists the centre in the directory,

81
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:25,390
along with its signing key and revocation list, so anyone can verify the
IDs it issues.

82
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:35,010
The hub also indexes choreographies: recurring workflows that several
people carry out together, each in its own repository.

83
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:38,720
murmurent choreography list shows what's published.

84
00:05:38,770 --> 00:05:41,500
Choreography install, followed by a name,

85
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:45,370
like the example, inhibition, sets one up for you.

86
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:47,960
Start your own with choreography init.

87
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:50,510
To publish it, push the repository,

88
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:54,560
and open a pull request that adds one row to the hub's index.

89
00:05:54,610 --> 00:05:58,140
Choreographies hold code and documentation only.

90
00:05:58,190 --> 00:06:01,460
Data stays in your centre's governed data root.

91
00:06:03,010 --> 00:06:03,840
Stuck?

92
00:06:03,890 --> 00:06:05,950
Just ask Claude Code.

93
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,887
Murmurent wires its own docs and commands into every session,

94
00:06:09,937 --> 00:06:13,510
so: walk me through installing Murmurent, really works.

95
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:17,070
Run murmurent doctor whenever something feels off.

96
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:21,400
Report bugs and request features on the murmurent_dev repository.

97
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:24,550
Issues on the public hub are turned off on purpose,

98
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:29,030
so never post personal details, or a join request, there.

99
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:34,300
To recap: install, run doctor, init, and adopt a repository.

100
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:42,580
Then enroll as a member, or join a centre as a PI The full documentation
is linked on screen.

101
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:44,850
Now, go and meet your agents.
